    "id": "train-7238",
    "question": "A man loves to go hiking.  He knows that he has to pack about .5 pounds of supplies for every mile he hikes.  He plans to go for a very long hike.  He knows that he can get 1 resupply during the hike that will be 25% as large as his first pack.  He can hike at a rate of 2.5 mph.  He is going to hike 8 hours a day for 5 days.  How much does he need to bring with his first pack?",
    "gold": "40",
    "answer": "He is going to hike 8*=40 hours\nThat means he will be hiking for 40*2.5=<<40*2.5=100>>100 miles\nSo he needs 100*.5=<<100*.5=50>>50 pounds of supplies\nWith the resupply he can get up to 1+.25=<<1+.25=1.25>>1.25 times his initial pack\nThat means his initial pack has to weigh 50/1.25=<<50/1.25=40>>40 pounds\n#### 40"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much the man needs to bring with his first pack, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total distance the man will hike:**\n   - The man hikes at a rate of 2.5 miles per hour.\n   - He plans to hike for 8 hours a day for 5 days.\n   - Total hours hiked = \\( 8 \\text{ hours/day} \\times 5 \\text{ days} = 40 \\text{ hours} \\).\n   - Total distance hiked = \\( 2.5 \\text{ miles/hour} \\times 40 \\text{ hours} = 100 \\text{ miles} \\).\n\n2. **Calculate the total amount of supplies needed:**\n   - The man needs 0.5 pounds of supplies for every mile he hikes.\n   - Total supplies needed = \\( 100 \\text{ miles} \\times 0.5 \\text{ pounds/mile} = 50 \\text{ pounds} \\).\n\n3. **Determine the size of the resupply:**\n   - The resupply is 25% as large as the first pack.\n   - Let \\( x \\) be the size of the first pack.\n   - The resupply size = \\( 0.25x \\).\n\n4. **Set up the equation for the total supplies:**\n   - The total supplies needed is the sum of the first pack and the resupply.\n   - \\( x + 0.25x = 50 \\).\n\n5. **Solve for \\( x \\):**\n   - Combine like terms: \\( 1.25x = 50 \\).\n   - Divide both sides by 1.25: \\( x = \\frac{50}{1.25} = 40 \\).\n\nTherefore, the man needs to bring \\(\\boxed{40}\\) pounds with his first pack.",
